{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Internal Peripheral Types"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use to talk about internal peripheral types."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Build the user interface, supported on the prototype assessment, determining the inputs and outputs required in the design and defining the navigation guidelines, according to the user's needs. Identify different hardware components and peripheral devices."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on the hardware devices and the architecture of a system to create the IT solution."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Simple Present Passive Affirmative Form"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\"> simple present passive </span> to give more importance to the object and the action in a sentence rather than to the subject.   "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Slots and cards which give you extra benefits are also included in this category."}, {"type": "example", "content": "External buses are connected to components outside the unit. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The <span class=\"strong\">simple present passive </span>  is used when the subject of the sentence can be omitted since it is implicit in the message. On the other hand, to mention the subject, you have to use <span class=\"strong\"> <span class=\"italic\">by </span> </span>  followed by it. </br></br> \t Let's compare these two sentences: </br></br>  <div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">Active voice: </span> </br></br>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> People </span>  use internal peripheral devices to improve a computer's performance. </span> </br></br>  <span class=\"strong\">Passive voice: </span> </br></br>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> Internal peripheral devices </span>  are used (by people) to improve their computer's performance. </div></span> </br></br>  As you can see, in passive voice, the subject of the sentence \u201cpeople\u201d is not necessary because it is implicit. </br></br>  This is the present simple passive structure: </br>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Object of the sentence </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">verb 'to be' </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">main verb in past participle</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">complement</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Peripheral devices </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">are </span></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"><span class=\\\"italic\\\">designed </span></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">to complement some features. </span></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Internal Peripheral Types"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\"> internal peripheral devices </span>  to give extra functions to a computer by adding them inside the case. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The most popular types of slots are PCI, PCI Express, PCMCIA and AGP."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They all share similar functions, although they also have individual characteristics."}, {"type": "example", "content": "On the other hand, we have types of cards which include sound cards, network cards and video cards."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Internal peripheral devices include different types of slots and cards that are connected to the computer thanks to a bus. They work in order to provide extra benefits to the computer. Let's take a look at some types of slots and cards: </br> </br>  <span class=\"strong\"> Types of slots: </span></br></br>  In this category we have Peripheral Component Interconnect (PCI), which is an advanced bus with the ability to include network cards, sound cards, and USB ports, among other features. In 2004, an upgraded version, PCI Express, was released. </br>  Another bus designed for this purpose was the PCMCIA, which stands for Personal Computer Memory Card International Association. Finally, we have the AGP that stands for Accelerated Graphics Port, used to attach graphic cards to a computer's motherboard. </br></br>  <span class=\"strong\"> Types of cards: </span></br></br>  In this category we have video cards, sound cards, and network cards. Video cards are also known as graphic cards. Besides generating images, they offer some add-ons such as the ability to connect more monitors, TV tuner adapter or even 3D graphics rendering. Sound cards facilitate the input and output of audio for multimedia applications. Finally, network cards are used to establish a network connection among devices to communicate. </br>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Types of slots</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Types of cards</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"PCI / PCI Express </br> PCMCIA</br> AGP</br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Video Card</br> Sound Card</br> Network Card </br>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bus "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "subsystem that transfers data to the computer"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You just probably need to add an expansion bus in your CPU. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob02aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "assemble"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to get items together for them to work "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You should assemble an expansion bus to connect a video card to run your game. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob02aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "slot"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a narrow space designed to insert something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The slots are designed to register the information that is provided by the card. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob02aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "processor"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "item that allows computers to function and process information"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They transfer data which travels to the processor and the motherboard inside a computer. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob02aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "card"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a thin piece that contains digital information"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The slots are designed to register the information that is provided by the card. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob02aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "analog"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when a digital device works with a continuous signal frequency"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You need to take into account the internal peripheral types; they transfer information to the computer digitally instead of using analog signals. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le01ob02aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about bus definition and internal peripheral types. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Represent a bus in a graphic and explain its parts. Don't forget to mention the internal peripheral types in your graphic."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your final product and explanation with your partners."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search information about bus definition and internal peripheral types."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I sketch a representation of the bus."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain in my graphic and the internal peripheral types to my partners."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe8n6le01ob02re2vid01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><span class=\"strong\"> Marianne: </span> I bought a new game, and I am looking forward to playing it, but my computer won't run it. </br>"}, {"time": "4200", "image": "", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Bennett: </span> You just probably need to add an expansion bus in your CPU. </br"}, {"time": "7200", "image": "", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Marianne: </span> What is that? </br>"}, {"time": "8200", "image": "", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Bennett: </span> A bus is a subsystem that connects different peripheral devices using the same sets of wires; they can be internal or external. Internal buses connect various components inside the CPU, and external buses are connected to components outside the unit. They transfer data which travels to the processor and the motherboard inside a computer. You should assemble an expansion bus to connect a video card to run your game. </br>"}, {"time": "31000", "image": "", "id": 4, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Marianne: </span> That sounds great! What else can I do to improve my computer? </br>"}, {"time": "34500", "image": "", "id": 5, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Bennett: </span> Well, you need to consider the internal peripheral types;  they transfer information to the computer digitally instead of using analog signals. Internal peripherals always go inside the computer case. Slots and cards which give you extra benefits are also included in this category. Even though they're optional, they are not ruled out.  </br>"}, {"time": "52000", "image": "", "id": 6, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Marianne: </span> Can you describe the types of slots and cards? </br>"}, {"time": "54400", "image": "", "id": 7, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Bennett: </span> Sure! The slots are designed to register the information that is provided by the card. The most popular types of slots are PCI, PCI Express, PCMCIA, and AGP. They all share similar functions, although they also have individual characteristics. On the other hand, we have different types of cards which include sound cards, network, cards and video cards. They offer certain features that allow you to do more things with your computer. </br>"}, {"time": "78600", "image": "", "id": 8, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Marianne:  </span> To sum up, I need to get an expansion bus with a slot that matches up with a good video card. Then, my game will work as I expect. </br>"}, {"time": "85800", "image": "", "id": 9, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Bennett: </span> You got it! </br>"}]}, "type": "video"}], "type": "video", "_data": [], "id": 3, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain what a bus is. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about internal peripheral types."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe types of slots and types of cards as part of the internal peripheral devices."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What can we find inside a computer's CPU?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What are the most common elements that you can include in a CPU to improve computer's performance?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Inside a Computer Case!"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0}, {"stimuli_ids": [3], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "te